  'html' => '<p>Welcome to the Asheville Regional Coalition for Home Repair\'s Help section. If you find yourself on here, you may be an employee, contractor, administrator, volunteer, or simply someone exploring in the future how this system works.</p>
<p>On September 28, 2024, our region was devastated by Hurricane Helene. Homes were completely uprooted in an instant. Many, many trees fell. We experienced, especially in our valleys and riverbound areas, flooding of up to 20 feet. We were not prepared for the level of complete destruction, nor would there have been any way to prepare. </p>
<p>In the aftermath, we saw neighbors organizing and meeting each other, like never before. And making sure that others were taken care of. The worst of a natural disaster brought out the best in people helping people. </p>
<p>Our coalition will cover disaster-related home repairs for qualifying households. Up to 50,000 dollars in  </p>
<p>This generosity extended to the level of non-profit institutions getting funding and forming partnership to enable projects like this. </p>
<p>Hurricane Helene was deemed a 10,000 year probability natural disaster and described in it\'s damages and devastation as \'biblical.\' We are seeing more and more of these extreme catastrophic natural disasters around the world. We wanted to take the system we built, and automate it with a platform. </p>
<p>Some aspirations with this tool:</p>
<ul>
<li>Create an automated system for every day people and organizations to provide aid after a natural disaster.</li>
<li>Have this tool be known about before a natural disaster comes to your region. </li>
<li>Make the process of mutual care after devastation some level of fun and game-like. There is nothing fun about the devastation and loss after a disaster, or repairing damaged roofing and drywall. But we believe game-ifying helping our neighbors survive the aftermath of a storm can bring out the best in us.</li>
</ul>
<p>Our existing home repair coalition is made possible by donors and partners, such as Cisco, Land of Sky, Habitat for Humanity, Community Housing Coalition of Madison County, PODER Emma....</p>
<p>Here are some helpful support documents you might be interested in reading next:</p>
<ul>
