<li><a href="help.php?doc=eligibility">Who Qualifies? Eligibility Determination &amp; Assuming Eligibility till proven otherwise</a> - Our process assumes eligibility until proven otherwise. Eligibility is based on income, home ownership, cause of damage, demographics, and geography.</li>
<li><a href="help.php?doc=metrics-math-money">Metrics, Math, and Money - How we make this all possible</a> - How donors, organizations, and everyday people who give a damn, make this all possible.</li>
</ul>
<p>Here\'s some more technical support items on how to get started:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><a href="help.php?doc=making-an-account">How do I make an account?</a> - The short answer is, you don\'t. There is not an option to register an account because that is not how this works. If you are in need of a home repair, you complete an intake form, and an account will be made for you at the end to track the status of your application. If you are looking to volunteer with us, we have a form for that as well that will generate a volunteer account. If you are a representative, employee, or administrator with a participating organization, we will make your accounts for you. For the public, there is a demo account you can log onto with placeholder data, so you can explore how the platform works. <a href="help.php?doc=making-an-account">Read more here</a></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><a href="help.php?doc=open-source-home-repair">This project is open-source - You can start one in your region before a disaster hits.</a> - As we develop, we are building an open source repository. This project is copylefted under <a href="https://opensource.org/license/gpl-3.0">GNU - General Public License</a>. This allows others access to the code and freedom to change and modify, as long as the project is being used for it\'s original intention. This repository is under construction, and not available publicly yet. But if you are interested in once it is available, you can sign up for our news list. <a href="help.php?doc=open-source-home-repair">Read more here</a></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><a href="help.php?doc=intake-privacy">What information do I need to provide in an intake for home repair assistance?</a> - To confirm eligibility, and to process an intake, we need certain information from applicants. Our goal is to only require the bare minimum information, and to not require more than that. Your privacy is important, and sometimes the less information we have on a private household, the better. But we do need to keep track of who lives there, who owns the home, the demographics data, household income, and geography. We will not share your private household information with law enforcement without a warrant, or with data brokers and ad agencies. Everything you share as an applicant is Protected and Privileged Information (PPI) under the [Privacy Act of 1974?].</p>
</li>
</ul>
